<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ===========================================================================================
       Consolidated architect categories.

       Merged in from Gideon's Clean Architect Tabs, which this mod replaces. That mod was pure XML,
       so nothing here needs the assembly and all of it works with the architect panel switched off.

       The problem these solve: RimWorld and its expansions scatter closely related buildings across
       categories that each hold two or three things, and every storage mod adds a category of its
       own. The result is a column of tabs where most are nearly empty, and where finding a shelf
       means remembering which mod supplied it.

       Three new categories collect them, and the patches in 1.6/Patches move the buildings across.
       Categories left empty afterwards are hidden rather than deleted wherever something else might
       still reference them: see ArchitectTabHider.xml for how, and why.

       Icons come from Textures/UI/ArchitectIcons, matched on defName rather than on label. Worth
       stating because the two differ here on purpose: the storage category is named UnifiedStorage
       and labelled "Storage", so its art file is UnifiedStorage.png. Naming it for the label is the
       mistake that leaves a category with no icon and no error to explain why.
       =========================================================================================== -->

  <!-- Research benches, which vanilla files under Misc alongside unrelated furniture.

       Order 60 puts it just after the building categories and before the zone and order tabs. -->
  <DesignationCategoryDef>
    <defName>Research</defName>
    <label>Research</label>
    <order>60</order>
    <specialDesignatorClasses>
      <li>Designator_Cancel</li>
      <li>Designator_Deconstruct</li>
    </specialDesignatorClasses>
  </DesignationCategoryDef>

  <!-- Everything to do with leaving the planet: Odyssey's gravship building, the vanilla ship parts,
       and the two orbital consoles that vanilla leaves in Misc.

       Only populated when Odyssey is installed, since that is the condition on the patch that fills
       it. Without Odyssey the vanilla Ship category survives untouched and this one stays empty,
       which means RimWorld does not draw it at all: a category with no designators is not Visible.

       Designator_RemoveFoundation is listed because gravship platforms need it and it is not one of
       the designators a category gets by default. -->
  <DesignationCategoryDef>
    <defName>Space</defName>
    <label>Space</label>
    <order>50</order>
    <specialDesignatorClasses>
      <li>Designator_Cancel</li>
      <li>Designator_Deconstruct</li>
      <li>Designator_RemoveFoundation</li>
    </specialDesignatorClasses>
  </DesignationCategoryDef>

  <!-- One home for shelves and containers, whichever mod supplied them.

       The defName is UnifiedStorage rather than Storage so it cannot collide with the category any
       one storage mod already defines. Several use "Storage" outright.

       Order 580 rather than something near the building categories: storage is placed and forgotten,
       so it belongs down with the tabs you reach for rarely, not between Structure and Furniture. -->
  <DesignationCategoryDef>
    <defName>UnifiedStorage</defName>
    <label>Storage</label>
    <order>580</order>
    <specialDesignatorClasses>
      <li>Designator_Cancel</li>
      <li>Designator_Deconstruct</li>
    </specialDesignatorClasses>
  </DesignationCategoryDef>

</Defs>
